{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "The clock, as colour. Each stop is a full set of theme tokens; the theme engine",
    "crossfades between two stops across a phase, so the room's colour is a readout of",
    "how much of the phase is left. Both themes are the same Ash Blue family.",
    "",
    "`hour` places the sun and the moon on their arc, and `starlight` is how much of the",
    "star field is showing. js/ui/sky.js paints from those two numbers, so the sky is",
    "the same clock the theme is - not a second one that could drift out of step.",
    "",
    "`mix` is how far the stop pulls the base palette towards its own hue.",
    "Every stop carries a full `light` and `dark` palette. Do not add a scalar field named `dark` - it will silently replace the palette and the whole app falls back to the light one."
  ],
